ated, if topics vary. Prerequisite: Junior standing required.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"67746","code":"2G","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["M","W"],"start":750,"end":825,"location":"123 English Building","instructors":["Garcia, G"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"SP27 CW 463 - Advanced Topics in Creative Writing - Gabriela Garcia - Writing Love and Friendship - In this advanced fiction course, we will analyze the techniques writers use to portray the complicated ways people come together—and apart—through close readings of fiction and poems by authors including Elena Ferrante, Toni Morrison, Gwendolyn Brooks, and Anne Carson. We will also consider philosophies and theories of love by writers such as Simone de Beauvoir, Roland Barthes, and Audre Lorde, and their utility in crafting believable relationships between characters. Finally, through generative exercises and assignments, students will produce their own short story that demonstrates intimacy as a function of craft."},{"crn":"67745","code":"2U","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["M","W"],"start":750,"end":825,"location":"123 English Building","instructors":["Garcia, G"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"SP27 CW 463 - Advanced Topics in Creative Writing - Gabriela Garcia - Writing Love and Friendship - In this advanced fiction course, we will analyze the techniques writers use to portray the complicated ways people come together—and apart—through close readings of fiction and poems by authors including Elena Ferrante, Toni Morrison, Gwendolyn Brooks, a